title Caravan abide -- the word an operator reads stands beside the reading held against it
prompt Keaton set the loop running: read Kyri and Radiant Style first, then REMEMBER, the itineraries, and the newest logs, close any open agent-closable red, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first and send it.
think Standfast first. The reds ledger reads 97 rows with %96 and %97 both CLOSED and rows 88-95 folded to the archive; no open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue is free.
think The running thread is the Caravan correction arc. The newest log's recommend named the question plainly: the record now holds two readings and resolves neither, which is honest, and leaves the next run to meet a quarrel it did not start.
think Read the record where it actually lands and the finding arrived on its own -- the disagreement rests in the plan's own notes, while an operator looking for the outcome opens a different file that reads exactly as it would have read had nobody objected.
think Named the rung abide under the Comlink tendency -- clear, fun, safe. Grepped abide, bide, heed, refer, pend, uphold across the tree; abide is free and the warmest of them, and the plan word Escort came with it.
think Council rota this lap: foundations/20260810-011514_pond-the-application-module.md, index taken as the choir count 64 mod 27 = 10. Wait -- 64 mod 27 is 10; the index read was 63 mod 27 = 9, the choir count before this rung landed, which is the honest lap index.
think Pond's line held for this rung: customs answers place, hold, or refuse at receipt, and the whole point is that a policy meets a running whole where the person is, rather than in a ledger they must already know to open.
think The design fork: an escort that argued would be a supervisor settling the quarrel it promised to leave open. So the mark quotes and never edits -- the plan's own published word stands untouched, and one byte of the reader's reading sits beside it.
think Four refusals by name, each about the mark rather than the word: AbideEarly the moment, AbideUnrecorded the supply, AbideMiscounted the count, AbideMisquoted the record.
think Proved five RED paths on metal before any GREEN claim, restoring the pristine file between each.
obs The dispute section came down to delegating wrappers rather than a second copy -- every fold of the rung below is reached through disputing_rung, which keeps one definition of what a disagreement is and lets this rung own only the reading of it.
obs Two of the four refusals were caught first by the pure folds in check_abide, before the run was ever reached. That is the happy zone working exactly as intended, and it took disarming the fold as well as the guard to prove the run refuses too.
obs The fifth RED is the one worth naming. With every guard disarmed and the mark quoting the plan's own reading, the run wrote c beside a word whose reader holds s -- the plan recorded as its own objector, and the selftest still calling itself GREEN. Seeing that once is what makes quotes a check rather than decoration.
obs Registered the rung in the choir in the same round, per REDS %81's lesson. The Caravan choir now sings 64 per-rung witnesses in one voice, roster bijection whole.
obs Added caravan/.abidings to the ignore roster beside its siblings, so a run's own notes never enter the tree.
loom witness=caravan_abide_witness phases=6 dependents=6 escorted=1 unattended_before=1 unattended_after=0 reds_proven=5 choir_rungs=64
loom module=caravan_abide lines=4993 asserts=268 usize=0
file caravan/abide.rye the rung -- one byte quoting the reader's objection, written where the settlement is read
file tools/caravan_abide_witness.rish the witness -- one plan run twice, the mark parting the two escorts, every note read outside the run that wrote it
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir registration, so the rung never sings unheard
file caravan/README.md the rung's own section and its module-table row
file .gitignore the note directory this rung writes under, ignored beside its siblings
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge, refilled with what is next
recommend keep-going the arc has answered for reach, repaired what a fall cost, taken back stale judgments, written to the reader those judgments misled, carried the letter, read the answer, recorded the disagreement, and now stands the published word beside it -- so the question above it is what a run owes a disagreement that never resolves at all: a mark says somebody objects, and says nothing about how long that objection may stand or what a plan does when the reader who made it never writes again.
